#: angular/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A standalone Angular app (via Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular`, no "
"Angular CLI) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"and\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(pantoken custom elements\n"
"for Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` calls `registerPantokenElements()` (from `@pantoken/"
"angular`) once at bootstrap so\n"
"  elements like `<instui-icon>` work in templates, and imports the token/"
"component CSS plus\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, and other component "
"behaviors out of the\n"
"  box).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` is a standalone component (`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` "
"lets the template\n"
"  compiler accept pantoken's custom element tags) whose template is styled "
"with `instui-*`\n"
"  classes; optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"are marked with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Una aplicación Angular independiente (vía Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-"
"angular`, sin Angular CLI) estilizada con\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"y\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(elementos personalizados de pantoken\n"
"para Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Desarrollar\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Qué hay aquí\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` llama a `registerPantokenElements()` (desde `@pantoken/"
"angular`) una vez en el arranque para que\n"
"  elementos como `<instui-icon>` funcionen en las plantillas, e importa el "
"CSS de tokens/componentes además de\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (configura modal, tooltip y otros comportamientos "
"de componentes listos para usar).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` es un componente independiente "
"(`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` permite que el compilador de plantillas\n"
"  acepte las etiquetas de elementos personalizados de pantoken) cuya "
"plantilla está estilizada con clases `instui-*`;\n"
"  los puntos de inserción opcionales (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"están marcados con\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Aplica clases como `class=\"instui-button\"` al marcado; consulta la\n"
"  [referencia de componentes](https://pantoken.app/api/css) para la lista "
"completa de clases.\n"
"\n"
"## Aprende más\n"
"\n"
"Consulta la [guía de inicio](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"para obtener más información.\n"

#: canvas-theme-editor/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Upload-ready assets for Canvas LMS's **Theme Editor**, plus a local preview "
"for authoring Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) page templates styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — upload these two files under **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** in Canvas.\n"
"  They're built for the CDN provider/theme/mode you chose when scaffolding "
"(`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light by default) and include a loader "
"for\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up component behaviors like modal, "
"tooltip, and drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — a local, TinyMCE-based editor (`npm run "
"dev`) that mirrors Canvas's\n"
"  RCE so you can author page templates against pantoken's classes before "
"copying them into Canvas.\n"
"  The page itself is built with pantoken's `wrapper` layout: click **Edit "
"theme** to open a tray\n"
"  with **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** tabs (CDN provider/theme/mode selects, "
"and syntax-highlighted,\n"
"  hand-editable copies of `theme.css`/`theme.js` that feed the live "
"preview), and the **?** button\n"
"  for full instructions. Use the **Layouts** toolbar button to start from "
"one of pantoken's bundled\n"
"  starter page layouts (hero, callout, two-column, rubric note, "
"testimonial), sourced from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"This opens a Vite dev server with:\n"
"\n"
"- An **editor** pane (TinyMCE, matching the version/config\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) itself "
"uses — see below).\n"
"  Use the **Layouts** button to load one of the bundled starter layouts "
"(this replaces the whole\n"
"  document, after a confirm, rather than inserting at the cursor), and the "
"**Source code** toggle\n"
"  to hand-edit the raw HTML in a syntax-highlighted (CodeMirror) view "
"alongside the editor, with\n"
"  the preview pane updating live as you type — unlike TinyMCE's stock `code` "
"plugin, which edits in\n"
"  a one-shot modal dialog with no live preview.\n"
"- A **preview** pane showing the editor's content with the current CSS/JS "
"tab's stylesheet/script\n"
"  applied (not just the resolved CDN URLs), wrapped to match Canvas's own "
"content-area background\n"
"  and max width — a faithful \"what this will look like once uploaded to "
"Canvas\" check, updated\n"
"  live as you type or edit the theme.\n"
"- The editor and preview panes sit in a split view you can resize by "
"dragging the divider, stack\n"
"  vertically instead of side by side, and swap the order of (drag a pane's "
"toolbar onto the other,\n"
"  or use the **Swap panes** button). Each pane has its own fullscreen "
"button.\n"
"- The **Edit theme** tray's **Config** tab holds the CDN provider/theme/mode "
"selects and\n"
"  **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js** links; its **CSS**/**JS** "
"tabs are editable copies\n"
"  of the generated files — hand-edit them and the preview picks up your "
"changes directly. Changing\n"
"  a Config select re-generates the CSS/JS tabs unless you've already edited "
"them, in which case a\n"
"  **Regenerate from config** button appears instead of silently overwriting "
"your edit.\n"
"\n"
"## Workflow\n"
"\n"
"1. Upload `theme.css` and `theme.js` to Canvas's Theme Editor (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) so\n"
"   pantoken's classes are available on every page.\n"
"2. Run `npm run dev`, use **Layouts** to start from a bundled starter, and "
"edit it like you\n"
"   would in Canvas's own RCE.\n"
"3. Click **Copy HTML** and paste the result into a Canvas page's RCE (switch "
"to the HTML editor\n"
"   view first). Canvas sanitizes pasted HTML server-side — this scaffold "
"doesn't attempt to\n"
"   replicate that, so always verify the pasted result in Canvas (see \"Notes "
"on Canvas's RCE\"\n"
"   below).\n"
"\n"
"## Notes on Canvas's RCE\n"
"\n"
"The Canvas Rich Content Editor runs TinyMCE and sanitizes submitted HTML on "
"the server against an\n"
"allowlist (`gems/canvas_sanitize` in canvas-lms, kept in sync with TinyMCE's "
"own\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). What that allowlist means for "
"templates built here:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, and `aria-*` attributes are "
"allowed on every element —\n"
"  pantoken's `class=\"instui-*\"` styling hooks (and inline `style`, e.g. "
"for CSS anchor positioning)\n"
"  **do** survive being pasted and saved, contrary to older guidance in this "
"file. `<script>` tags\n"
"  are always stripped.\n"
"- **RCE-safe pantoken components**: static/display components — alert, view, "
"heading, text, table,\n"
"  a button-as-`<a>` (not a real `<button>`), blockquote. Stick to semantic "
"HTML pantoken already\n"
"  supports (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, headings, lists, tables).\n"
"- **RCE-unsafe**: anything from `@pantoken/interactions`'s behavior set — "
"modal, tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, or any other component driven by the native "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributes. Those attributes aren't in Canvas's "
"sanitizer allowlist, so\n"
"  the markup survives but the interactive behavior silently breaks the first "
"time the page is\n"
"  saved in Canvas, even with `theme.js`'s `@pantoken/interactions` loader "
"present. Real form\n"
"  elements (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) and "
"inline `<svg>` are\n"
"  stripped outright — none of the bundled starter templates use them.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` loads `@pantoken/interactions` from the CDN, which runs in "
"Canvas's global page scope —\n"
"useful for interactions on pages you build directly in Canvas's RCE with raw "
"HTML edits, but (per\n"
"above) any `popover`/`command`-attribute-driven markup pasted from the RCE "
"preview here won't stay\n"
"interactive once saved.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Activos listos para subir para el **Editor de Tema** de Canvas LMS, más una "
"vista previa local para crear plantillas de página del Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) estilizadas con\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## Qué hay aquí\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — sube estos dos archivos en **Editor de Tema → "
"Avanzado** en Canvas.\n"
"  Están construidos para el proveedor/theme/mode de CDN que elegiste al "
"crear el scaffold (`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light por defecto) e incluyen un cargador "
"para\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (conecta los comportamientos de los componentes "
"como modal, tooltip y drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — un editor local basado en TinyMCE (`npm run "
"dev`) que refleja el\n"
"  RCE de Canvas para que puedas crear plantillas de página usando las clases "
"de pantoken antes de copiarlas a Canvas.\n"
"  La página en sí está construida con el layout `wrapper` de pantoken: haz "
"clic en **Edit theme** para abrir una bandeja\n"
"  con pestañas **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** (selectores de proveedor/theme/"
"mode del CDN, y copias editables con resaltado de sintaxis de\n"
"  `theme.css`/`theme.js` que alimentan la vista previa en vivo), y el botón "
"**?** para instrucciones completas. Usa el botón de la barra de herramientas "
"**Layouts** para empezar desde uno de los layouts de página incluidos de "
"pantoken (hero, callout, two-column, rubric note, testimonial), extraídos "
"de\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Desarrollo\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Esto abre un servidor de desarrollo Vite con:\n"
"\n"
"- Un panel **editor** (TinyMCE, coincidiendo con la versión/config\n"
"  que usa [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-"
"lms) — ver abajo).\n"
"  Usa el botón **Layouts** para cargar uno de los layouts incluídos (esto "
"reemplaza todo el\n"
"  documento, tras confirmar, en lugar de insertarlo en el cursor), y el "
"conmutador **Source code**\n"
"  para editar manualmente el HTML crudo en una vista con resaltado de "
"sintaxis (CodeMirror) junto al editor, con\n"
"  la vista previa actualizándose en vivo mientras escribes — a diferencia "
"del plugin `code` de TinyMCE, que edita en\n"
"  un diálogo modal de una sola vez sin vista previa en vivo.\n"
"- Un panel **preview** que muestra el contenido del editor con la hoja de "
"estilos/script de la pestaña CSS/JS actual\n"
"  aplicada (no solo las URLs resueltas del CDN), envuelto para coincidir con "
"el fondo del área de contenido y el ancho máximo de Canvas — una "
"verificación fiel de \"cómo se verá esto una vez subido a Canvas\", "
"actualizada\n"
"  en vivo mientras escribes o editas el tema.\n"
"- Los paneles de editor y vista previa están en una vista dividida que "
"puedes redimensionar arrastrando el divisor, apilar\n"
"  verticalmente en lugar de lado a lado, y cambiar el orden de ellos "
"(arrastra la barra de herramientas de un panel sobre el otro,\n"
"  o usa el botón **Swap panes**). Cada panel tiene su propio botón de "
"pantalla completa.\n"
"- La bandeja **Edit theme** en su pestaña **Config** contiene los selectores "
"de proveedor/theme/mode del CDN y\n"
"  los enlaces **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js**; sus pestañas "
"**CSS**/**JS** son copias editables\n"
"  de los archivos generados — edítalos a mano y la vista previa aplicará tus "
"cambios directamente. Cambiar\n"
"  un selector de Config re-genera las pestañas CSS/JS a menos que ya las "
"hayas editado, en cuyo caso aparece un\n"
"  botón **Regenerate from config** en lugar de sobrescribir silenciosamente "
"tu edición.\n"
"\n"
"## Flujo de trabajo\n"
"\n"
"1. Sube `theme.css` y `theme.js` al Editor de Tema de Canvas (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) para que\n"
"   las clases de pantoken estén disponibles en cada página.\n"
"2. Ejecuta `npm run dev`, usa **Layouts** para empezar desde un starter "
"incluido, y edítalo como lo harías\n"
"   en el propio RCE de Canvas.\n"
"3. Haz clic en **Copy HTML** y pega el resultado en el RCE de una página de "
"Canvas (primero cambia a la vista del editor HTML).\n"
"   Canvas sanitiza el HTML pegado del lado del servidor — este scaffold no "
"intenta\n"
"   replicar eso, así que siempre verifica el resultado pegado en Canvas (ver "
"\"Notas sobre el RCE de Canvas\"\n"
"   abajo).\n"
"\n"
"## Notas sobre el RCE de Canvas\n"
"\n"
"El Rich Content Editor de Canvas ejecuta TinyMCE y sanitiza el HTML enviado "
"en el servidor contra una\n"
"lista permitida (`gems/canvas_sanitize` en canvas-lms, mantenida en "
"sincronía con las propias\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements` de TinyMCE). Lo que esa lista "
"permitida significa para las plantillas creadas aquí:\n"
"\n"
"- Los atributos `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role` y `aria-*` están "
"permitidos en cada elemento —\n"
"  los hooks de estilo `class=\"instui-*\"` de pantoken (y `style` en línea, "
"p. ej. para posicionamiento de anclas en CSS)\n"
"  **sí** sobreviven al pegarse y guardarse, contrariamente a guías "
"anteriores en este archivo. Las etiquetas `<script>`\n"
"  siempre se eliminan.\n"
"- Componentes de pantoken seguros para RCE: componentes estáticos/"
"visualización — alert, view, heading, text, table,\n"
"  un botón como `<a>` (no un verdadero `<button>`), blockquote. Mantener "
"HTML semántico que pantoken ya\n"
"  soporta (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, headings, lists, tables).\n"
"- No seguros para RCE: cualquier cosa del conjunto de comportamientos de "
"`@pantoken/interactions` — modal, tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, o cualquier otro componente impulsado por los "
"atributos nativos `popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor`. Esos atributos no están en la lista permitida del "
"sanitizador de Canvas, por lo que\n"
"  el marcado sobrevive pero el comportamiento interactivo se rompe "
"silenciosamente la primera vez que la página se\n"
"  guarda en Canvas, aun con el cargador `@pantoken/interactions` de "
"`theme.js` presente. Elementos de formulario reales\n"
"  (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) y `<svg>` en "
"línea son\n"
"  eliminados por completo — ninguna de las plantillas starter incluidas los "
"usa.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` carga `@pantoken/interactions` desde el CDN, que se ejecuta en el "
"ámbito global de la página de Canvas —\n"
"útil para interacciones en páginas que construyas directamente en el RCE de "
"Canvas con ediciones HTML crudas, pero (como se indicó\n"
"arriba) cualquier marcado impulsado por atributos `popover`/`command` pegado "
"desde la vista previa del RCE aquí no permanecerá\n"
"interactivo una vez guardado.\n"

#: components/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A plain TypeScript app (via Vite) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructure's\n"
"design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` holds the actual page markup — a `wrapper`-layout shell from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). View source\n"
"  and edit it directly; nothing is injected by JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` imports `@pantoken/css` (defines every `--instui-*` custom "
"property),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (document defaults + focus ring), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` classes), `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, "
"and other component\n"
"  behaviors out of the box), and your own `src/style.css` — add interactive "
"behavior here.\n"
"- Optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) are marked "
"with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` in `index.html` — replace their contents with "
"your own markup.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [HTML guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Una aplicación TypeScript sencilla (vía Vite) con estilo usando\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), los tokens de diseño\n"
"y los iconos de Instructure.\n"
"\n"
"## Desarrollar\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Qué hay aquí\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` contiene el marcado real de la página — una estructura tipo "
"`wrapper` de\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). Ver el origen\n"
"  y editarlo directamente; nada es inyectado por JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` importa `@pantoken/css` (define cada propiedad personalizada "
"`--instui-*`),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (valores por defecto del documento + "
"anillo de foco), `components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` clases), `@pantoken/interactions` (conecta modal, tooltip y "
"otros comportamientos de componentes listos para usar), y tu propio `src/"
"style.css` — añade comportamiento interactivo aquí.\n"
"- Los puntos de inserción opcionales (encabezado, filtros, contenido, final) "
"están marcados con\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` en `index.html` — reemplaza su contenido con tu "
"propio marcado.\n"
"- Aplica clases como `class=\"instui-button\"` al marcado; consulta la\n"
"  [referencia de componentes](https://pantoken.app/api/css) para la lista "
"completa de clases.\n"
"\n"
"## Aprende más\n"
"\n"
"Consulta la [guía de HTML](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) para "
"obtener más información.\n"

#: next/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A Next.js (App Router) app styled with [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"Instructure's design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` wraps the config with `withPantoken(...)` (adds pantoken "
"to\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` imports `@pantoken/css`, which defines every `--instui-*` "
"custom\n"
"  property, at the root so it's available on every page, plus the `wrapper` "
"layout's root class on\n"
"  `<body>` and `PantokenInteractions` (a client component that loads "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  wires up modal, tooltip, and other component behaviors out of the box).\n"
"- `app/page.tsx` renders markup styled with `instui-*` classes; optional "
"insertion points (header,\n"
"  filters, content, trailing) are marked with `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Una aplicación Next.js (App Router) estilizada con [`@pantoken/next`]"
"(https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"los tokens de diseño e iconos de Instructure.\n"
"\n"
"## Desarrollar\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Qué hay aquí\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` envuelve la configuración con `withPantoken(...)` (añade "
"pantoken a\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` importa `@pantoken/css`, que define cada propiedad "
"personalizada `--instui-*`,\n"
"  en la raíz para que esté disponible en cada página, además de la clase "
"raíz del diseño `wrapper` en\n"
"  `<body>` y `PantokenInteractions` (un componente del cliente que carga "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  configura modal, tooltip y otros comportamientos de componentes listos "
"para usar).\n"
